From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: guineveresaenger <guinevere@pulumi.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 10:21:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add shim package exposing the provider constructors

The Plugin Framework provider is constructed by internal/framework.NewProvider,
which Go's internal package rule makes unreachable from the Pulumi provider
module. Pulumi needs that value to build a muxed SDKv2 + Plugin Framework shim
via pkg/pf/tfbridge.MuxShimWithDisjointgPF, so re-export it from a package that
lives inside this module.

NewSDKProvider is re-exported alongside it so both halves of the mux are
obtained from one place; signalfx.Provider is already exported and could be
called directly.

The patch can be removed once upstream exposes a Plugin Framework constructor
outside of internal/. Removing it before then breaks compilation of
provider/resources.go, which is the signal that it is still needed.

diff --git a/shim/shim.go b/shim/shim.go
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..522b4f94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/shim/shim.go
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+// Package shim exposes the upstream provider constructors to the Pulumi bridge.
+//
+// The Plugin Framework provider lives in an internal package, so it is only
+// reachable from within this module.
+package shim
+
+import (
+	pfprovider "github.com/hashicorp/terraform-plugin-framework/provider"
+	sdkschema "github.com/hashicorp/terraform-plugin-sdk/v2/helper/schema"
+
+	internalframework "github.com/splunk-terraform/terraform-provider-signalfx/internal/framework"
+	"github.com/splunk-terraform/terraform-provider-signalfx/signalfx"
+)
+
+func NewSDKProvider() *sdkschema.Provider {
+	return signalfx.Provider()
+}
+
+func NewFrameworkProvider(version string) pfprovider.Provider {
+	return internalframework.NewProvider(version)
+}
